kDir":10,"totalRaces":98},"recordContext":{"menRecords":["overall"],"menPreviousRecord":{"time":"05:29:14","holder":"Alan ROBB","year":1978,"type":"overall"},"womenRecords":["down"],"womenPreviousRecord":{"time":"07:04:59","holder":"Cheryl WINN","year":1982,"type":"down"},"womenWouldHaveWonMen":{"mostRecentYear":1952,"mensWinner":"Trevor ALLEN","mensTime":"07:00:02"}},"narrative":"The 1984 Comrades Marathon was the 59th running of the race, run in the 'down' direction from Pietermaritzburg to Durban over 89.750 km. The race was held on Friday, 1 June. Conditions: Very cold at start, warm and cloudless by mid morning. Runners had 11 hours to complete the course.\n\nBruce FORDYCE claimed the men's title in 05:27:18, ahead of Bob DE LA MOTTE (05:30:59) and Chris REYNEKE (05:34:39). Lindsay WEIGHT won the women's race in 06:46:35, followed by Priscilla CARLISLE (07:15:32).\n\nBruce FORDYCE's 05:27:18 set a new course record, beating Alan ROBB's 05:29:14 from 1978. Lindsay WEIGHT set a new women's down record of 06:46:35, surpassing Cheryl WINN's 07:04:59 from 1982. Lindsay WEIGHT's 06:46:35 was faster than the men's winning time as recently as 1952 (Trevor ALLEN, 07:00:02).\n\nFrom a field of 7,105 entries, 7,103 runners crossed the finish line (100.0% completion rate), with athletes representing over 17 countries. The field comprised 6,841 men and 262 women (3.7% female). The average finish time was 09:10:43.\n\nMedals awarded: 11 Gold, 932 Silver, 6,160 Bronze. 2,825 runners (39.8%) were completing their first Comrades. The final finisher was Swiss-Bear BAUMGARTNER in 10:59:59.\n\nCompared to the previous down run in 1982, the field was 54.5% larger.\n\nVeterans and masters athletes made up 24% of the finishers, with 5,393 seniors (avg 09:08:37) and 1,709 in the veteran categories.","countryDataPct":100.0}